ans believe that they are  surrounded by enemies and therefore have  to be prepared to defend the homeland  they often even draw parallels with the  attack on the soviet union in the second  world war and naturally from the comfort  of our sofas in our homes we can think  how exaggerated is this putin but the  truth is that this message does resonate  in russian society it really does in a  recent survey conducted by the levada  center for sociological research look at  what the second concern of russian  citizens is  more than half of russians are really  panicking about the possibility of a  world war not a war in ukraine but a  full-scale world war it is evident that  the russian propaganda around the  besieged fortress story is having an  effect and that's why headlines like  this one are always music to the  kremlin's ears  nato countries urge to supply more  weapons to ukraine  the pretext putin needs to do as he  pleases is that of security and alleged  threats because come on obviously most  ordinary russians don't want a war  rations are like you and me they want to  work they want prosperity they want  freedom  [Music]  but naturally that patriotism that has  been instilled by the kremlin for  decades makes russians feel obliged to  defend their russian brothers in the  donbass  the successful annexation of crimea in  2014 boosted russian patriotism and at  the same time it was useful for putin to  conceal from his own people that the  russian economy was no longer growing at  the same pace as it was at the beginning  of the century so given what we have  seen it should come as no surprise that  the kremlin is trying to repeat the move  with a russia hit by pandemics inflation  and corruption allegations in other  words we cannot rule out that the whole  conflict is a genuine diversionary  maneuver  certainly there was not many other  reasons but having come to this point  it's your turn what's your take on the  attack on ukraine leave us your comments  be